{"name":"Caribbean Current","hex":"#006e6e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"current","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The generally unidirectional movement of a gas or fluid.","The part of a fluid that moves continuously in a certain direction, especially  ellipsis of ocean current."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Existing or occurring at the moment.","Generally accepted, used, practiced, or prevalent at the moment; having currency."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/current"}],"entries":[{"title":"Caribbean Current","blocks":[{"text":"The Caribbean Current is a warm ocean current that transports significant amounts of water and flows northwestward through the Caribbean from the east along the coast of South America and into the Gulf of Mexico. The current results from the flow of the Atlantic South Equatorial Current as it flows north along the coast of Brazil. As the current turns north through the Yucatán Channel, it is renamed the Yucatán Current. The Caribbean Current water comes from the Atlantic Ocean via the North Equatorial, North Brazil, and Guiana Currents. The circulation of the Columbia-Panama Gyre flows counter-clockwise to the Caribbean Current."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Map_of_the_Caribbean-Greater_Antilles.png/330px-Map_of_the_Caribbean-Greater_Antilles.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caribbean_Current"},{"title":"Caribbean","blocks":[{"text":"The Caribbean is a geo-political region in the middle of the Americas centered around the Caribbean Sea in the North Atlantic Ocean, mostly overlapping with the West Indies. Bordered by North America to the north and also the west through Central America, and South America to the south, it comprises numerous islands, cays, islets, reefs, and banks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Central_America_and_the_Caribbean_Shaded_Relief_Map.png/330px-Central_America_and_the_Caribbean_Shaded_Relief_Map.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caribbean"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Caribbean_current.png/500px-Caribbean_current.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Caribbean_current.png/500px-Caribbean_current.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Caribbean current, a warm ocean current in Caribbean Sea","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACaribbean_current.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg/500px-Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg/1280px-Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg/500px-Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAtlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/13/Languages_of_the_Caribbean.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/13/Languages_of_the_Caribbean.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Pre-Columbian languages of the West Indies. Ciboney Taíno, Classic Taíno, and Iñeri were Arawakan, Karina and Yao were Cariban. Macorix, Ciguayo and Guanahatabey are unclassified.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALanguages_of_the_Caribbean.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/The_Battle_of_the_Saints%2C_12_April_1782_RMG_BHC0444.jpg/500px-The_Battle_of_the_Saints%2C_12_April_1782_RMG_BHC0444.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/The_Battle_of_the_Saints%2C_12_April_1782_RMG_BHC0444.jpg/1280px-The_Battle_of_the_Saints%2C_12_April_1782_RMG_BHC0444.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/The_Battle_of_the_Saints%2C_12_April_1782_RMG_BHC0444.jpg/500px-The_Battle_of_the_Saints%2C_12_April_1782_RMG_BHC0444.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Battle of the Saintes between British and French fleets in 1782, by Nicholas Pocock","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Battle_of_the_Saints%2C_12_April_1782_RMG_BHC0444.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Attack_near_Playa_Giron._April_19%2C_1961._-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Attack_near_Playa_Giron._April_19%2C_1961._-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Attack_near_Playa_Giron._April_19%2C_1961._-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Attack_near_Playa_Giron._April_19%2C_1961._-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Counter-attack by Cuban Revolutionary Armed Forces supported by T-34 tanks near Playa Giron during the Bay of Pigs Invasion, 19 April 1961.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAttack_near_Playa_Giron._April_19%2C_1961._-_panoramio.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Tectonic_plates_Caribbean.png/500px-Tectonic_plates_Caribbean.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Tectonic_plates_Caribbean.png/500px-Tectonic_plates_Caribbean.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":".mw-parser-output .legend{page-break-inside:avoid;break-inside:avoid-column}.mw-parser-output .legend-color{display:inline-block;min-width:1.25em;height:1.25em;line-height:1.25;margin:1px 0;text-align:center;border:1px solid black;background-color:transparent;color:black}.mw-parser-output .legend-text{}  The Caribbean plate is the reason islands exist here. On the north, obduction has scraped rocks onto the North American plate (such as in western Cuba). On the east, the Lesser Antilles subduction zone produces volcanism and an island arc. Complex interactions with the South American plate has created islands along the southern boundary. Coral islands are found in insular Colombia near the east coast of Central America.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATectonic_plates_Caribbean.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Johny_Cay.jpg/500px-Johny_Cay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Johny_Cay.jpg/1280px-Johny_Cay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Johny_Cay.jpg/500px-Johny_Cay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tropical monsoon climate in San Andrés island, Caribbean, Colombia.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJohny_Cay.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Tobacco_field_cuba1.jpg/500px-Tobacco_field_cuba1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Tobacco_field_cuba1.jpg/500px-Tobacco_field_cuba1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A field in Pinar del Rio planted with Cuban tobacco","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATobacco_field_cuba1.jpg"}],"sounds":{"current":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1a/En-uk-currant.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/1/1a/En-uk-currant.ogg/En-uk-currant.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0e/En-us-ne-current.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/0e/En-us-ne-current.ogg/En-us-ne-current.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/56/En-us-current.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/56/En-us-current.ogg/En-us-current.ogg.mp3"}]}}}